  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "Evidence: Multi-profile RNA with PCA_n2000 + avgpool (config_002, acc 0.591) substantially outperforms single-profile (config_001, acc 0.485), confirming that profile aggregation is a high-impact design choice. Image-only (config_010, acc 0.208) is very weak, so the RNA pathway is the primary signal source and must be optimized before multimodal fusion is informative. Uncertainty: We do not yet know whether transformer aggregation outperforms simple avgpool for combining multiple profiles—this is the next most consequential architectural decision after establishing that multi-profile helps. This experiment (config_003) changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding everything else at the best-known RNA settings (PCA_n2000, multi-profile), making it a clean, minimal test of one variable. It is the best use of the next budget slot because it directly extends the strongest configuration, reduces uncertainty on a design axis that will propagate into all multimodal experiments, and avoids the confound of simultaneously changing encoder, profile setting, and fusion strategy."
}

